// D1576 — the value is a NEVER-FILLED `const x = null`. `x = null` binds
// `mkNullableTy(-1)`, the A-infer-null hole, filled in place by the first non-null
// assignment; with no assignment the `-1` inner flows on, so the binding is not `T | null`
// for any `T`. Its type is the `null` type and its rep is `nullref` (D1567's `nulnone`), the
// bottom of the GC hierarchy — one value, a subtype of every nullable ref valtype, which is
// what lets one cell serve a struct / string / list / map / closure destination with no
// coercion. Before this row the cell was an i32 holding 0: check-clean INVALID WASM at every
// ref destination, and a present-looking value at the i32-repped ones.
//
// THE SETUP DECLARES IT IN THE DELIVERY'S OWN SCOPE, so each position exercises the storage
// class it actually has there — a function local, a start-fn local, a module global.
//
// The PROOF reads THROUGH the narrow (`v.a`), so a cell delivered at the wrong heap type
// traps or refuses rather than passing.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/matrix.py, whose docstring is the spec.
// @@PRELUDE@@
type C = { a: i32, b: i32 }
// @@SETUP@@
const __nn = null
// @@VALUE@@
__nn
// @@TYPE@@
C | null
// @@TEST@@
v != null
// @@HIT@@
print(v.a)
// @@MISS@@
print("none")
// @@WANT@@
none
// @@SKIP@@
map_value: a map whose VALUE is `null` cannot be told from a missing key — the read's `!= null` guard is false either way, so the proof prints nothing at both seeds
